# أسئلة Senior مهمة

### Why is semantic HTML better than generic `<div>` elements?

> Semantic elements communicate the purpose and structure of content to browsers, assistive technologies, developers, and search engines.
> 

### Why shouldn't a `<div>` be used as a button?

> It does not provide the native semantics, keyboard behavior, focus behavior, and accessibility features of a real button.
> 

### Can IDs be duplicated?

> IDs should be unique within a document.
> 

### Why should form controls have labels?

> Labels provide an accessible name and establish a clear association between the label and the form control.
> 

### Why shouldn't HTML elements be chosen based on visual appearance?

> HTML should represent semantic meaning, while CSS should control presentation.
> 

### When should you use `<a>` vs `<button>`?

> Use `<a>` for navigation and `<button>` for actions.
> 

